    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) headlining our offensive strategy. Facing a favorable 4.71 xERA matchup against Chandler, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** thrives due to a massive platoon advantage and the elite leadoff projection. He remains our primary engine for the scarce Stolen Base category. We also find high-floor value in **Trea Turner** (75.36) and **Yordan Alvarez** (70.49). **Trea Turner** benefits from an optimized #2 spot and a soft matchup against Holmes, while **Yordan Alvarez** overcomes a tougher opponent in Peralta by sheer force of his elite 0.443 xwOBA, acting as the stabilizer for our RBI and HR projections. \n\n**Colt Keith** (68.51) and **Junior Caminero** (67.39) round out our most potent tier, with **Colt Keith** seeing a significant boost from his prime #3 position against Hughes, capitalizing on the pitcher's vulnerability. **Lars Nootbaar** (65.03) is also a strong start, as his platoon advantage and leadoff billing leverage the park factor in his favor. The most difficult benching decision involved **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (40.50), who narrowly missed the cut. While his underlying metrics are respectable, the high efficiency scores of our starters\u2014specifically the platoon-heavy profiles of **Christian Yelich** and **Kazuma Okamoto**\u2014pushed **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** to the pine to avoid burning game caps on a marginal return.\n\nRisks remain, however, particularly with **Carson Benge** (46.11), who faces the toughest arm on our board in Schlittler (2.88 xERA). While **Carson Benge** maintains a startable grade due to a decent platoon edge, the SP skill variance makes him our highest volatility play. Meanwhile, **Gary Sanchez** (41.84) and **Dillon Dingler** (49.35) sit at the bottom of our active rotation; **Gary Sanchez** is hampered by a tough draw against Burns, and we are monitoring the lineup stability for **Dillon Dingler** and **Chase Meidroth** to ensure they maintain their projected spots. We remain clear of the IL-ridden **Casey Schmitt**, **Josh Smith**, and **Jacob Gonzalez**, keeping the roster focused on active, high-leverage production.",
